 of key intermediates (rxn_001, rxn_004, rxn_010). While each reaction individually reflects credible chemistry, the failure to conserve atoms precludes approval.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_001\",\n        \"rxn_004\",\n        \"rxn_010\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Balance transformations explicitly.\",\n        \"Include or clarify additional reactants/products as needed.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.4\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.7,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.82,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.97,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.85,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.74,\n      \"feedback\": \"P8, omitting photoreduction, represents a plausible but less thoroughly demonstrated variation. Core transformations are maintained, but rxn_004\u2019s atom imbalance persists. Chemistry otherwise fits with variant non-photochemical Strecker repercussions.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_004\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Fix atom/charge balancing for critical intermediate formation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.4,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.4,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.3,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.9\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.6,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.8,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.92,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.85,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.68,\n      \"feedback\": \"P9 features an integrated formose-cyanide pathway. As with P1 and P3, balancing is faulty at